# A full adder built from nothing but transistors, resistors and LEDs: it adds three bits, A, B and a
# carry in C, into a sum S and a carry out, as each column of a binary adder does.
#
# It is nine NOR gates in resistor–transistor logic, the logic of the Apollo guidance computer. Each
# gate is one transistor whose collector is pulled up to 5 V through 1 kΩ: either input high pushes
# current through its 10 kΩ into the base, the transistor saturates, and the output falls to a tenth
# of a volt; both inputs low, the transistor is off and the output sits high.
#
#     n1 = A nor B                         the carry when both are 1, inverted, and more
#     n2 = A nor n1,  n3 = B nor n1
#     n4 = n2 nor n3                       A xnor B
#     n5 = n4 nor C
#     n6 = n4 nor n5,  n7 = C nor n5
#     S  = n6 nor n7                       (A xnor B) xnor C, which is A xor B xor C
#     Co = n1 nor n5                       A and B, or C and (A xor B)
#
# The signals run along the bus at the top; each gate takes its two inputs down from it and sends its
# output back up. Flip the switches: the LEDs light for S and for the carry out.

speed 1m
start settled

battery   B1    0 12  0 21  5V
wire            0 12  72 12
wire            0 21  73 21
ground          0 21

# The inputs: a switch to 5 V, and a pulldown that holds the input low while the switch is open.
switch    A     2 12  2 14  open
resistor  RA    2 14  2 21  10k
wire            2 14  3 14
wire            3 14  3 1
switch    B     5 12  5 14  open
resistor  RB    5 14  5 21  10k
wire            5 14  6 14
wire            6 14  6 2
switch    C     8 12  8 14  open
resistor  RCI   8 14  8 21  10k
wire            8 14  9 14
wire            9 14  9 3

# The bus: A, B, C and the gates' outputs n1 to n7, each from its source to its last reader.
wire            3 1   19 1
wire            6 2   26 2
wire            9 3   54 3
wire            17 4  68 4
wire            24 5  33 5
wire            31 6  34 6
wire            38 7  47 7
wire            45 8  69 8
wire            52 9  61 9
wire            59 10 62 10

# n1 = A nor B
resistor  RC1   16 12 16 15  1k
npn       Q1    16 15 14 17  16 19
wire            16 19 16 21
resistor  R1A   13 14 13 17  10k
resistor  R1B   12 14 12 17  10k
wire            12 17 14 17
wire            13 1  13 14
wire            12 2  12 14
wire            16 15 17 15
wire            17 15 17 4

# n2 = A nor n1
resistor  RC2   23 12 23 15  1k
npn       Q2    23 15 21 17  23 19
wire            23 19 23 21
resistor  R2A   20 14 20 17  10k
resistor  R2B   19 14 19 17  10k
wire            19 17 21 17
wire            20 4  20 14
wire            19 1  19 14
wire            23 15 24 15
wire            24 15 24 5

# n3 = B nor n1
resistor  RC3   30 12 30 15  1k
npn       Q3    30 15 28 17  30 19
wire            30 19 30 21
resistor  R3A   27 14 27 17  10k
resistor  R3B   26 14 26 17  10k
wire            26 17 28 17
wire            27 4  27 14
wire            26 2  26 14
wire            30 15 31 15
wire            31 15 31 6

# n4 = n2 nor n3
resistor  RC4   37 12 37 15  1k
npn       Q4    37 15 35 17  37 19
wire            37 19 37 21
resistor  R4A   34 14 34 17  10k
resistor  R4B   33 14 33 17  10k
wire            33 17 35 17
wire            34 6  34 14
wire            33 5  33 14
wire            37 15 38 15
wire            38 15 38 7

# n5 = n4 nor C
resistor  RC5   44 12 44 15  1k
npn       Q5    44 15 42 17  44 19
wire            44 19 44 21
resistor  R5A   41 14 41 17  10k
resistor  R5B   40 14 40 17  10k
wire            40 17 42 17
wire            41 3  41 14
wire            40 7  40 14
wire            44 15 45 15
wire            45 15 45 8

# n6 = n4 nor n5
resistor  RC6   51 12 51 15  1k
npn       Q6    51 15 49 17  51 19
wire            51 19 51 21
resistor  R6A   48 14 48 17  10k
resistor  R6B   47 14 47 17  10k
wire            47 17 49 17
wire            48 8  48 14
wire            47 7  47 14
wire            51 15 52 15
wire            52 15 52 9

# n7 = C nor n5
resistor  RC7   58 12 58 15  1k
npn       Q7    58 15 56 17  58 19
wire            58 19 58 21
resistor  R7A   55 14 55 17  10k
resistor  R7B   54 14 54 17  10k
wire            54 17 56 17
wire            55 8  55 14
wire            54 3  54 14
wire            58 15 59 15
wire            59 15 59 10

# S = n6 nor n7, lighting its LED when high
resistor  RC8   65 12 65 15  1k
npn       Q8    65 15 63 17  65 19
wire            65 19 65 21
resistor  R8A   62 14 62 17  10k
resistor  R8B   61 14 61 17  10k
wire            61 17 63 17
wire            62 10 62 14
wire            61 9  61 14
wire            65 15 66 15
led       S     66 15 66 21  green

# Co = n1 nor n5, lighting its LED when high
resistor  RC9   72 12 72 15  1k
npn       Q9    72 15 70 17  72 19
wire            72 19 72 21
resistor  R9A   69 14 69 17  10k
resistor  R9B   68 14 68 17  10k
wire            68 17 70 17
wire            69 8  69 14
wire            68 4  68 14
wire            72 15 73 15
led       CO    73 15 73 21  yellow

label     n1    17 15
label     n2    24 15
label     n3    31 15
label     n4    38 15
label     n5    45 15
label     n6    52 15
label     n7    59 15
label     sum   66 15
label     carry 73 15
